{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>From a false matter.</b> It speaks with respect to the judge: that he not render a false judgment. Its parallel is צדק צדק תרדוף, \"Justice, justice you shall pursue\" (ibid. 16:20)." "<b>And the clear and the righteous do not slay.</b> In that matter — if you know he is wicked in another matter, do not say: since he did thus, a severe wickedness, I will kill him and remove the stumbling block from the path, for I, even I, will exact judgment from him and he will not escape My hand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:34.504024570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}